./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Custom-Templates.md:205:**Can I export one line per report?**
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Custom-Templates.md:207:No, the custom template always exports one line per expense. At the moment it is not possible to create a template that will export one line per report.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Default-Export-Templates.md:6:Use default export templates for exporting report data to a CSV format, for data analysis, or  uploading to an accounting software.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Default-Export-Templates.md:10:- **All Data - Report Level Export** - This export prints a line per report, giving a summary of the report data.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Default-Export-Templates.md:11:- **Basic Export** - A simpler expense level export without as much detail. This exports the data visible on the PDF of the report. Basics such as date, amount, merchant, category, tag, reimbursable state, description, receipt URL, and original expense currency and amount.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Default-Export-Templates.md:12:- **Canadian Multiple Tax Export** - Exports a line per expense with all available info on the taxes applied to the expenses on your report(s). This is useful if you need to see the tax spend.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Default-Export-Templates.md:13:- **Category Export** - Exports category names with the total amount attributed to each category on the report. While you can also access this information on the Insights page, it can be convenient to export to a CSV to run further analysis in your favorite spreadsheet program.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Default-Export-Templates.md:14:- **Per Diem Export** - This exports basic expense details only for the per diem expenses on the report. Useful for reviewing employee Per Diem spend.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Default-Export-Templates.md:15:- **Tag Export** - Exports tag names into columns with the  total amount attributed to each tag on the report.
