./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Create-a-report-approval-workflow.md:2:title: Create a report approval workflow
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Create-a-report-approval-workflow.md:19:   - **Submit and Close**: No approval is required. Once a report is submitted, it will be automatically approved and closed. This option may be useful if your expense approvals occur in another system or if the submitter and approver are the same person.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Create-a-report-approval-workflow.md:20:   - **Submit and Approve**: All reports go to one person that you assign as the approver. Once a report is submitted, it is sent to the approver. This is the default option.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Create-a-report-approval-workflow.md:21:   - **Advanced Approval**: Allows for more complex workflows, like assigning different [approvers](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees) for different employees or requiring secondary approvals for expenses that exceed a [set limit](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Require-review-for-over-limit-expenses).
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Set-a-random-report-audit-schedule.md:2:title: Set a random report audit schedule
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Set-default-report-title.md:2:title: Set default report title
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Set-default-report-title.md:7:Workspace Admins can set a default report title for all reports created under a specific workspace. If desired, these titles can also be enforced to prevent employees from changing them.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Set-default-report-title.md:13:5. Configure the formula. You can use the example provided on the page as a guide or choose from more [report formula options](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/spending-insights/Custom-Templates).
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Set-default-report-title.md:14:   - Some formulas will automatically update the report title as changes are made to the report. For example, any formula related to dates, total amounts, and workspace name would adjust the title before the report is submitted for approval. Note that changes to Report Field values reflected in the Report Title (i.e., `{field:Customer}`) will not be reflected in the title of Open reports until submission. Between submission and approval, changes will update the title immediately. Changes will **not** retroactively update report titles for reports that have been Approved or Reimbursed.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Require-review-for-over-limit-expenses.md:26:When over-limit approvals are set for a specific member, a secondary approver will be required when the member submits a report that contains expenses exceeding the limit amount. If the member is an approver for other members’ reports, the approval limit applies to those reports as well.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Require-review-for-over-limit-expenses.md:31:To set expense limits for specific workspace members, your workspace must use Advanced Approvals as the report approval workflow.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Require-review-for-over-limit-expenses.md:39:5. In the “If report total is over” field, enter the amount that will require this member’s reports to need a secondary review. This limit also applies to reports that the member is in charge of reviewing.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:5:Approval workflows can get complex. Let’s look at the lifecycle of an expense report from submission to final approval.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:8:The approval workflow for all reports starts as soon as the report is submitted. Reports can be submitted manually or set to [submit automatically](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Automatically-submit-employee-reports) by Concierge.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:10:If you change part of your workflow after a report has been submitted, the workflow for that report will not change unless it is retracted and resubmitted.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:13:If you have [special approvers for categories or tags](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-tag-and-category-approvers) that are added to a report, the report will go to these people for approval first. They will be notified about the report via email or an in-app notification.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:16:The report will now travel through the approval workflow for the workspace:
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:17:- Submit & Close: If you use a [Submit & Close](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Create-a-report-approval-workflow) workflow, the report will now close and notify the set person.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:18:- Submit & Approve: If you use a [Submit & Approve](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Create-a-report-approval-workflow) workflow, the report will now go to the set person for their approval.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:19:- Advanced Approval: If you use an [Advanced Approval](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Create-a-report-approval-workflow) workflow, the report will now go to the person in the submitter’s “Submits to” column of the Workspace Members table. Once that person approves the report,
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:20:    - The report then goes to the person in the approver’s Approves To column.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:21:    - If the approver has an [approval value limit](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Require-review-for-over-limit-expenses) (i.e. they have approval restrictions based on the total amount of the report), the report will go to the set person.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:22:    - The report continues through the approval workflow until it reaches someone who does not have anyone in their Approves To column. This person is the final approver.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:24:Once the report receives final approval, it may be exported to a [connected accounting software](https://help.expensify.com/expensify-classic/hubs/connections/) and/or reimbursed.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:27:If you’ve chosen to [require manual approval for expenses that exceed a set limit](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Require-review-for-over-limit-expenses), any report that doesn’t contain a single expense over this amount will be approved by Concierge.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:38:Pat does the accounting for a small engineering firm. Everyone submits their reports to Pat for approval. However, all plant and equipment purchases must be seen by Dale. They created a category called “3005 Plant and Equipment” and assigned Dale as the category approver. This way, when a report is coded with this category, it will go to Dale once it is submitted. Then Pat will receive the report for final approval, reimbursement, and to export it to their accounting software connection.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:45:Her sales rep David regularly hosts client meetings, which results in a report filled with coffee, lunch, and parking expenses paid for on his company card. David has dutifully SmartScanned his receipts and coding them after each purchase. None of the individual expenses are over $100, so his report submits itself on Sunday evening. The report is instantly final approved within moments of submission, and the report history notes that Concierge both submitted and final approved the report.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:50:Amal is a photojournalist for a major magazine, and they have been traveling for a week. The last report they submitted contains meals, accommodations, and emergency camera equipment.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:51:1. Their report first goes to Tony, head of photography, who is the category approver for the “6050 Cameras and AV” category that was added to Amal’s report.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:52:2. The report then goes to Jamie, who is Amal’s manager and “submits to.”
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:53:3. Jamie approves and forwards the report to her “approves to” person, which is her manager Ali.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:54:4. Ali approves and forwards the report to his “approves to” person, which is the finance team.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:55:5. The finance team is the final approver for the report. They check the coding, approve the report, export it to the accounting system, and reimburse Amal.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:60:Amal had another travel week, but this time to Hong Kong. Their report total includes a $1,200 flight as well as $950 for accommodations and food.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/How-Complex-Approval-Workflows-Work.md:62:The report goes to Jamie for approval, but Jamie has an “If Report Total is Over $2000 then Approves To” rule that requires large expenses to be approved by Lee. That means once Jamie approves the report, Lee must approve the expense next. Once Lee approves, the report goes to the finance team who completes the final approval.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-tag-and-category-approvers.md:7:Once your workplace has created tags and categories, approvers can be assigned to them. Tag and category approvers are automatically added to the report approval workflow when a submitted expense contains a specific tag or category.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-tag-and-category-approvers.md:9:For example, if all employees are required to tag project-based expenses with a tag for the project, you can assign the project manager as the approver for that tag. This way, when a report is submitted containing expenses with that project tag, it will first be routed to the project manager for approval before continuing through the rest of the approval workflow.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-tag-and-category-approvers.md:11:If a report contains multiple categories or tags that each require a different reviewer, then each reviewer must review the report before it can be submitted. The report will first go to the category approvers, the tag approvers, and then the approvers assigned in the approval workflow.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:2:title: Assign report approvers to specific employees
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:8:To assign different approvers for different employees, your workspace must use Advanced Approvals as the report approval workflow.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:11:To assign different approvers for different employees (instead of everyone submitting to the same person), your workspace must use Advanced Approval as the report approval workflow.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:13:To assign a report approver to a specific member of your workspace,
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:26:    - Approves To: Determines who must approve a report after this user has approved it. This creates an approval chain. When added, a note is visible in the Details column of the Workspace Members table. If blank, the user is a “final approver.”
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:27:    - If Report Total is Over $X then Approves To: These two fields add an extra approver if the report total exceeds the set amount. When added, a note is visible in the Details column of the Workspace Members table.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:44:- Employee doesn’t approve any reports. When they submit a report, it goes to Manager 1 for approval.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:45:- After Manager 1 approves a report from the Employee, the report goes to Manager 2 for approval unless the report is over $1,000. In that case, it goes directly to the Finance Team.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:46:- When Manager 1 submits their own report, it goes to the Finance Team for approval.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:47:- When Manager 2 approves a report or submits their own report, it goes to the Finance Team for approval.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/reports/Assign-report-approvers-to-specific-employees.md:48:- When the Finance Team submits a report, it is approved by the Finance Team. They are the final approver.
